  [1mThe main decision:[0m the page is built from the template components in [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m ([38;5;153mpageHeader[39m, [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m, [38;5;153mselectField[39m,
  [38;5;153mdataTable[39m, [38;5;153mstatusChip[39m, [38;5;153memptyState[39m), the same way [38;5;153moverview.js[39m does it. It deliberately doesn't copy [38;5;153mservices.js[39m, which
  writes its own table, [38;5;153mpill[39m classes, escaping and inline [38;5;153monchange[39m. The components already cover what the spec asks for:
  - sorting both ways, with header links and [38;5;153maria-sort[39m
  - keeping the sort in hidden fields when the filter changes
  - submitting the form when the dropdown changes
  - green, amber, red and blue chips

  So the plan needs no new CSS, no new JS, and no changes to the vendored [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m.

  [1mTasks:[0m
  1. [1mPage code[0m ([38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[39m, plus 12 tests): [38;5;153mrenderDeploys(snapshot, query)[39m and [38;5;153mformatDuration()[39m. The tests
     cover the header, column order, newest-first default, both sorts in both directions, the four chips, the duration
     format and "running", the filter keeping the sort, sort links keeping the filter, the empty state, and unknown
     query values falling back.
  2. [1mRoute and nav link:[0m one entry in [38;5;153mROUTES[39m in [38;5;153msrc/server.js[39m and one "Deploys" link after "Services" in [38;5;153msrc/layout.js[39m.
     Three server tests: the page renders inside the layout, a missing snapshot gives a 503, and a half-written snapshot
     gives a 503. The last step loads the page in the running app.

  [1mChoices the spec doesn't settle:[0m
